  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1158 PM CDT THU OCT 15 2026\n\nThis evening we have a cold front extending from the Great Lakes\nSWWD to AR and swinging back into Central TX. This front should\nget enough of a favorable push from the upper flow to move\nthrough C AL and finally allow fall to make its arrival in the\narea on Friday. There may be just enough moisture with the help\nof frontal forcing to allow for a few isolated showers Friday\nafternoon and evening. No TS or heavy rain is anticipated.\n\nHowever, before the front moves through, we will still see enough\nwarming Friday for max temps to be above normal going into the\n80s. The exception may be in the far NW counties where there will\nbe less time to heat up before the front arrives where it may not\nget out of the 70s. Breezy and gusty at times NRLY winds should\nbe felt Friday afternoon, that night and on into Saturday with\ntight surface pressure gradients behind the front. Cool fall\nreadings are on tap with lows in the 40s for many on Friday night\nand for all Saturday/Sunday nights with highs generally in the\n60s over the weekend. Our airmass should begin to moderate for\nnext week as our flow becomes more ERLY, but overall still dry\nwith Eastern Conus surface ridging.\n\n08",
